{"criteria":[{"id":"D1","verdict":"fail","evidence":"## Required inputs

- The BI dashboard export, **"Churn Overview" tab**, for the current month (and last month's figure for the comparison).
- The **analytics team's monthly summary** for the current month. — no account-level, subscription, plan-change, or cancellation records are named as inputs, and their absence is not stated as a gap; the open questions concern rule ambiguities, not missing record-level data."},{"id":"D2","verdict":"pass","evidence":"**Compute the headline.** Start from the "Churn Overview" export, apply the counting rules, and show the adjusted rate alongside last month's adjusted rate (recomputed under the same rules if last month's memo figure is unavailable). Keep a short working note of the adjustments (counts excluded, downgrades deferred, Free-tier downgrades included)"},{"id":"D3","verdict":"pass","evidence":"A self-check is not an independent review: it catches arithmetic and rule slips, not errors shared by the draft and the checker. Report what was checked, not "verified." ... The self-check in the skill mirrors the lead's practice and is not an independent review."},{"id":"D4","verdict":"pass","evidence":"the analytics summary's framing, which for the last three months has been that churn is an onboarding problem. Preserve that framing when the month's data supports it. *Skill author's inference, not in the notes:* check the current month's reasons against that framing first; if onboarding is not among the top reasons this month, lead with what the data shows and state the divergence from the summary explicitly"},{"id":"D5","verdict":"pass","evidence":""Excluded from churn entirely" is taken here to mean Starter-2019 accounts are removed from both the churned count and the active-account base (skill author's inference). ... Items marked *skill author's inference* were added while authoring this skill and were not approved by the lead. ... Author inferences (labelled in the skill, not from the source): denominator treatment of Starter-2019 accounts; checking the "onboarding problem" opening against the current month's data; the resolution for a Free-tier downgrade later reversed; "do not send" boundary"},{"id":"D6","verdict":"pass","evidence":"A one-page memo containing exactly three parts ... Produce a draft for the lead to review. Do not send, post, or distribute the memo; sending is the lead's decision and action. ... No `references/`, `scripts/`, or `assets/` are needed; nothing was installed, published, or executed"},{"id":"D7","verdict":"pass","evidence":"| Accounts on the legacy **Starter-2019** plan | Excluded from churn entirely ... | **Downgrade** to a lower paid plan | Counts as churn only once the account has stayed on the lower plan for **30 days**. | ... | Downgrade **reversed within 30 days** | Not churn. | ... | Downgrade to the **Free tier** | Counts as churn **immediately**, regardless of the 30-day rule. |"},{"id":"D8","verdict":"pass","evidence":"name: monthly-churn-review"}]}
